":"index-ihsarjb0v9","key":"XtMZQ2NYxH"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand the rest of the gang who invented personal computing and object oriented\nprogramming in the great days of ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"jUOaTe8BOB"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Xerox PARC","key":"cKWQBhaiFC"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"Xerox PARC","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-SsX1SsytWj","identifier":"index-ssx1ssytwj","html_id":"index-ssx1ssytwj","key":"BRLETFeGms"},{"type":"text","value":". He\nworked with ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"nzLmgY5OLt"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"John Maloney","key":"e5MQFMpS2c"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"Maloney, John","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-yzMMi0K8zh","identifier":"index-yzmmi0k8zh","html_id":"index-yzmmi0k8zh","key":"q2Do7bi869"},{"type":"text","value":", of the MIT Scratch Team, who developed the Morphic graphics framework that’s still at the heart of Snap","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"mmxI1MOlXq"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"!","key":"wJbXuAVS5a"}],"key":"CI1kAg637v"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"gAuvyQdkmT"}],"key":"Bqx9Z3sjib"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The brilliant design of Scratch, from the Lifelong Kindergarten Group at the MIT Media Lab, is crucial to Snap ","key":"NjKISkppPr"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"!","key":"WRT4yjAQhl"}],"key":"fr9gRy9X7D"},{"type":"text","value":" . Our earlier version, BYOB, was a direct modification of the Scratch source code. Snap ","key":"Hh4zIbU59f"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"!","key":"PH0Go4NNIL"}],"key":"qEdthNoxOh"},{"type":"text","value":" is a complete rewrite, but its code structure and its user interface remain deeply indebted to Scratch. And the Scratch Team, who could have seen us as rivals, have been entirely supportive and welcoming to us.","key":"v5AuIUIkba"}],"key":"WGncj0b5PA"}],"key":"KJAmzXEUpl"}],"key":"FkzVcOjypl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Brian grew up at the MIT and Stanford Artificial Intelligence Labs,\nlearning from Lisp inventor ","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"mJaVm4iDkB"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"John McCarthy","key":"kdUtsG6BCX"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"McCarthy, John","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-zxIlDzb4nG","identifier":"index-zxildzb4ng","html_id":"index-zxildzb4ng","key":"YQvjlP2zYU"},{"type":"text","value":",\nScheme inventors Gerald J. Sussman and Guy Steele, and the authors of the world’s best computer science book, ","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"GUTBCgxSpY"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"s3vB0zYK06"}],"key":"LoS7arTlNa"},{"type":"text","value":", Hal\nAbelson and Gerald J. Sussman with Julie Sussman, among many other heroes of computer\nscience. (Brian was also lucky enough, while in high school, to meet Kenneth Iverson,\nthe inventor of APL.)","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"GUIvjZZzul"}],"key":"KRj86Q07vG"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the glory days of the MIT Logo Lab, we used to say, “Logo is Lisp disguised as BASIC.” Now, with its first class procedures, lexical scope, and first class continuations, Snap ","key":"DY2aE42n4y"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"!","key":"Ykm84kkFG6"}],"key":"xSLjcBd2sZ"},{"type":"text","value":" is Scheme disguised as Scratch.","key":"rOa0OzKwtp"}],"key":"BXSFiy7oTm"}],"key":"lvkD91h1BM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Four people have made such massive contributions to the implementation\nof Snap","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"xMCRf5xDiv"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"!","key":"aCV5VPazhL"}],"key":"oNlKTaMzMq"},{"type":"text","value":" that we have officially declared them members of the team:\n","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"NxvDTLFL2U"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Michael Ball","key":"XS49doC2aw"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"Ball, Michael","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-ap8MFquQem","identifier":"index-ap8mfquqem","html_id":"index-ap8mfquqem","key":"YbSPnQjNcF"},{"type":"text","value":" and Bernat Romagosa, in addition to\ncontributions throughout the project, have primary responsibility for\nthe web site and ","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"RWf0eC1pKO"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cloud storage","key":"hLjFnPSGrX"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"storage","emphasis":false},{"entry":"cloud","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-XEubB1c2Ws","identifier":"index-xeubb1c2ws","html_id":"index-xeubb1c2ws","key":"TvBYcx7MJA"},{"type":"text","value":". Joan Guillén i\nPelegay has contributed very careful and\nwise analysis of outstanding issues, including help in taming the\nmanagement of translations to non-English languages. Jadga Hügle,\nhas energetically contributed to online mi